    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0641" n="631" xml:id="pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/2396</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 5629</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-06">November 6, 1937</date>.<lb/>[Received November
                        8.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to recent reports
                    regarding the affectation of American-owned lands in the Yaqui Valley, Sonora,
                    particularly despatches numbers 5616 and 5617, dated November 2 and 4, 1937,
                    respectively.</p>
                <p>There is enclosed a translation of note number 312538 of November 6, 1937, from
                    the Foreign Office on the subject. A translation of the enclosure to that note
                    is also enclosed.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d627-a1.xml" xpointer="d627-a1"/>
